From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:49:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: drop a monitor-only frame after monitor delivery

With a monitor up, ieee80211_rx_monitor() consumes a frame that
should_drop_frame() rejects only where exactly one monitor takes it.
Two or more monitors get a copy, and a monitor that does not take the
frame gets nothing. In both cases the function returns the original
frame, and __ieee80211_rx_handle_packet() processes it, since it reads
none of the flags that should_drop_frame() tests. A frame with
RX_FLAG_ONLY_MONITOR, for example one that the driver marked for a
failed PN check or an ICV error, thus reaches the stack.

Free such a frame after the monitors received it, like the branch for
no monitor does, so that the number of monitors does not decide whether
a frame goes on to the RX path.

Fixes: 127f60bfa98f ("mac80211: rewrite monitor mode delivery logic")
Fixes: f92e0cf19ae0 ("wifi: mac80211: filter on monitor interfaces based on configured channel")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -978,6 +978,11 @@ ieee80211_rx_monitor(struct ieee80211_lo
 	if (!origskb)
 		return NULL;
 
+	if (only_monitor) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(origskb);
+		return NULL;
+	}
+
 	return ieee80211_clean_skb(origskb, present_fcs_len, rtap_space);
 }
 
